\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {IV}{\ignorespaces Angular power spectrum of the chirality asymmetry map (Catalog~C, equivariant). The first row is the canonical \emph  {single-mode} $\ell \!=\!1$ post-MASTER result that anchors the dipole-parity null (companion artifact \texttt  {master\_results/master\_power\_spectrum.json}, $\ell _1$\,dipole entry; analysis subsample $n\!=\!5{,}547{,}858$, $f_{\rm  sky}\!=\!0.659$). Rows 2--5 are five-mode \emph  {bandpowers} $\ell \!\in \![\ell _{\rm  eff}\!-\!2,\,\ell _{\rm  eff}\!+\!2]$ from the canonical-$N$ MASTER recompute on the full $N_{\rm  spiral}\!=\!3{,}201{,}160$ / $f_{\rm  sky}\!=\!0.491$ analysis (companion artifact \texttt  {r42\_results/wave\_14\_pp\_namaster\_verification.json}; $500$ MC realizations). $\sigma _{\rm  null}$ is the per-bin standard deviation of the MC null distribution at that bandpower. Higher-bandpower $\sim \!2\sigma $ values reflect residual coupling of the $9.5\sigma $ monopole into low-$\ell $ bandpowers under the partial-sky MASTER kernel; the dipole-parity observable is the single-mode $\ell \!=\!1$ result (first row), and the bandpower table is a null-consistency cross-check at multipoles \emph  {other than} the dipole. A single canonical-$N$ MASTER recompute at $\ell \!=\!1$ on the equivariant map is on the post-arXiv-submission TODO; the two analyses use the same Catalog~C CW/CCW labels and differ only in the analysis mask and normalization, so agreement is expected but not numerically verified at the time of this release.}}{14}{table.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:multipole}{{IV}{14}{Angular power spectrum of the chirality asymmetry map (Catalog~C, equivariant). The first row is the canonical \emph {single-mode} $\ell \!=\!1$ post-MASTER result that anchors the dipole-parity null (companion artifact \texttt {master\_results/master\_power\_spectrum.json}, $\ell _1$\,dipole entry; analysis subsample $n\!=\!5{,}547{,}858$, $f_{\rm sky}\!=\!0.659$). Rows 2--5 are five-mode \emph {bandpowers} $\ell \!\in \![\ell _{\rm eff}\!-\!2,\,\ell _{\rm eff}\!+\!2]$ from the canonical-$N$ MASTER recompute on the full $N_{\rm spiral}\!=\!3{,}201{,}160$ / $f_{\rm sky}\!=\!0.491$ analysis (companion artifact \texttt {r42\_results/wave\_14\_pp\_namaster\_verification.json}; $500$ MC realizations). $\sigma _{\rm null}$ is the per-bin standard deviation of the MC null distribution at that bandpower. Higher-bandpower $\sim \!2\sigmaunit $ values reflect residual coupling of the $9.5\sigmaunit $ monopole into low-$\ell $ bandpowers under the partial-sky MASTER kernel; the dipole-parity observable is the single-mode $\ell \!=\!1$ result (first row), and the bandpower table is a null-consistency cross-check at multipoles \emph {other than} the dipole. A single canonical-$N$ MASTER recompute at $\ell \!=\!1$ on the equivariant map is on the post-arXiv-submission TODO; the two analyses use the same Catalog~C CW/CCW labels and differ only in the analysis mask and normalization, so agreement is expected but not numerically verified at the time of this release}{table.4}{}}
