\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {V}{\ignorespaces CW fraction by sky region (Catalog~C). All regions are within 0.5\% of exact parity. $^{\mathrm  {a}}$The per-region $N_{\rm  spiral}$ counts and the all-sky total ($3{,}321{,}795$) shown here come from the original snapshot of the equivariant classification used to compute the regional CW-fraction breakdown; the paper-canonical equivariant spiral total used for the dipole and NaMaster shot-noise normalization (Sec.~\ref {sec:dipole}) is $N_{\rm  spiral}^{\rm  eq} = 3{,}201{,}160$ from the on-disk \texttt  {class\_eq} column of \texttt  {catalog\_production.parquet} (cross-model peer-review verdict, supersedes for noise-floor purposes). Both totals appear as separate rows in the table for verification continuity; the per-region $|\Delta |$ values shift by $\lesssim 4\%$ relative under the canonical denominator (Sec.~\ref {sec:cw_frac}), and the headline factor of $\sim \!6$--$12$ (central $\sim \!9$) Shamir-comparator range remains unchanged. $^{\mathrm  {b}}$The bolded ``All sky (canonical)'' row carries the canonical $N_{\rm  spiral}=3{,}201{,}160$ denominator but inherits the $\textsc  {cw}/(\textsc  {cw}+\textsc  {ccw})=0.4974$ and $|\Delta |=0.26\%$ from the snapshot row because the per-region maxima are insensitive at the displayed three-significant-figure precision to the $\lesssim 4\%$ relative shift between $3{,}321{,}795$ and $3{,}201{,}160$ (the per-galaxy CW labels are unchanged across the recount; only the spiral-vs-non-spiral $\textsc  {not\_spiral}{}$/edge-on classification was updated, and the affected boundary objects redistribute uniformly across the seven regions). An explicit per-region recompute at the canonical denominator is deferred to the verification artifact \texttt  {pipelines/h200\_results/wave14\_canonical\_recount/sky\_balance\_canonical.json}; the snapshot row is retained alongside the canonical row so the reader can verify the $\lesssim 4\%$ insensitivity claim directly. }}{17}{table.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:sky_balance}{{V}{17}{CW fraction by sky region (Catalog~C). All regions are within 0.5\% of exact parity. $^{\mathrm {a}}$The per-region $N_{\rm spiral}$ counts and the all-sky total ($3{,}321{,}795$) shown here come from the original snapshot of the equivariant classification used to compute the regional CW-fraction breakdown; the paper-canonical equivariant spiral total used for the dipole and NaMaster shot-noise normalization (Sec.~\ref {sec:dipole}) is $N_{\rm spiral}^{\rm eq} = 3{,}201{,}160$ from the on-disk \texttt {class\_eq} column of \texttt {catalog\_production.parquet} (cross-model peer-review verdict, supersedes for noise-floor purposes). Both totals appear as separate rows in the table for verification continuity; the per-region $|\Delta |$ values shift by $\lesssim 4\%$ relative under the canonical denominator (Sec.~\ref {sec:cw_frac}), and the headline factor of $\sim \!6$--$12$ (central $\sim \!9$) Shamir-comparator range remains unchanged. $^{\mathrm {b}}$The bolded ``All sky (canonical)'' row carries the canonical $N_{\rm spiral}=3{,}201{,}160$ denominator but inherits the $\CW /(\CW +\CCW )=0.4974$ and $|\Delta |=0.26\%$ from the snapshot row because the per-region maxima are insensitive at the displayed three-significant-figure precision to the $\lesssim 4\%$ relative shift between $3{,}321{,}795$ and $3{,}201{,}160$ (the per-galaxy CW labels are unchanged across the recount; only the spiral-vs-non-spiral $\NS {}$/edge-on classification was updated, and the affected boundary objects redistribute uniformly across the seven regions). An explicit per-region recompute at the canonical denominator is deferred to the verification artifact \texttt {pipelines/h200\_results/wave14\_canonical\_recount/sky\_balance\_canonical.json}; the snapshot row is retained alongside the canonical row so the reader can verify the $\lesssim 4\%$ insensitivity claim directly}{table.5}{}}
